WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
JIM WALDO: Do you know how
to ethically collect and use

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.130
personal data for your business?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:09.120
By gathering this data, you
have taken on a responsibility

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.010
to protect the privacy of
those whose data you gather.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.460
In data privacy and
technology, we will consider

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.150
the many definitions of privacy and
their implications for individuals,

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.360
corporations, and governments.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.640
We will explore what personal privacy
means, how data is collected and used,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.080
the trade-offs between privacy and
other values, and look to the future.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.660
ANDY YEN: Your data can
and will outlive you.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.170
It will be there forever.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.595
It just seems ridiculous to not try
to protect this most valuable asset.

00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:44.070
MIKE SMITH: This course
is crucial for businesses

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.040
today because of the
changing nature of our world.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.070
You will immerse yourself in
real-world challenges faced

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.060
by industry-leading experts, and explore
the legal and ethical implications

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.145
of collecting user and customer data.

00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:59.400
ALASTAIR MACTAGGART: When you
think about it in a larger sense,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.272
our personal information really is
the fuel for these corporations.

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:05.730
LATANYA SWEENEY: There are just
so many different interests

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.290
in so many different issues.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.350
It's not just how do I
deliver anonymous data.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.950
MIKE SMITH: Privacy is a complex
and multifaceted concept.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.410
By the end of the course,
you should be able to apply

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:19.690
your learning to your life,
your role, and your business.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.860
It's time to learn how to
balance the utility of a data set

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.960
with the privacy of the individuals.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.820
Do you agree to enroll in this course?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.270
[MUSIC PLAYING]

